<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="AllTheThingsYouAre-Ab-Theme" spTempo="88">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1939
Composer:	Jerome Kern
Lyricist:	Oscar Hammerstein II
Form:	36-bar ABCD
Style:	Swing
Key:	Ab major

“All the Things You Are” was written for the 1939
 Broadway musical Very Warm for May, Jerome
 Kern’s final Broadway show. Its unusually sophisticated
 harmony moves through several temporary key centers,
 while the commonly played refrain expands the usual
 32-bar song form to 36 bars; the original verse is now
 rarely performed. </spComments>
